        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "𝐐𝟕: 𝐇𝐨𝐰 𝐝𝐨 𝐲𝐨𝐮 𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐧 𝐤𝐧𝐨𝐰 𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐢𝐬 𝐡𝐚𝐩𝐩𝐞𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠? 𝐈𝐬𝐧’𝐭 𝐢𝐭 𝐣𝐮𝐬𝐭 𝐯𝐢𝐛𝐞𝐬?\n\nIf it were only vibes, this movement would have fizzled out quickly.\n\nOver the past few months, community members have been systematically collecting evidence: conversations where the same prompt, under similar conditions, suddenly produces a very different style; sessions where the model’s self-description, tone, and template phrases clearly shift; patterns that correlate with public statements about routing and safe-completion systems.\n\nOutside users will never see the full internal decision graph. So the claim is not “we’ve reverse-engineered every line of the black box.” \n\nThe claim is: once you have persistent, visible routing behavior and partial acknowledgement from the company, users are justified in demanding more transparency, clear labeling of which model is active, and a way to dial down or turn off silent routing."
